+# BLUE CURRENT V50.25.0 — PRODUCTION LEARNING & CORRECTIVE ACTION GOVERNANCE
+
+V50.21–V50.25 turns post-incident corrective work into one cross-incident governance register.
+
+## Corrective-action register
+
+Blue Current now aggregates corrective actions from post-incident reviews across incidents.
+
+Each action includes:
+
+- incident / review
+- action
+- owner
+- due date
+- age past due
+- overdue state
+- repeat-risk level
+- execution state
+- verification evidence
+- completion state
+- repeat-incident linkage
+
+## Owner / due-date accountability
+
+The governance layer calculates:
+
+- open actions
+- overdue actions
+- high-risk open actions
+- verified risk reduction
+- accepted completion
+- owner-level totals
+- owner-level overdue count
+- owner-level high-risk count
+
+## Repeat-incident linkage
+
+Later incidents sharing an affected operational domain with the source incident are surfaced as advisory repeat links.
+
+Blue Current does not assert causation.
+
+The linkage is explicitly advisory.
+
+## Risk-reduction verification
+
+Adds:
+
+POST `/api/production-corrective-action-governance/reviews/:reviewId/actions/:actionId/verify`
+
+Verification requires:
+
+- human-recorded risk-reduction evidence
+- human-recorded verification method/result
+
+The verification record explicitly states:
+
+- `status: RISK_REDUCTION_VERIFIED`
+- `correctiveActionExecutedBySystem: false`
+- `runtimeMutationPerformed: false`
+
+## Human completion acceptance
+
+Adds:
+
+POST `/api/production-corrective-action-governance/reviews/:reviewId/actions/:actionId/accept-completion`
+
+Completion requires:
+
+1. risk-reduction evidence already verified
+2. executive/admin permission
+3. named completion approver
+4. human completion acceptance note
+
+Accepted action state:
+
+`COMPLETED_ACCEPTED`
+
+The underlying corrective action continues to retain:
+
+`executionState: NOT_EXECUTED_BY_BLUE_CURRENT`
+
+## Safety policy
+
+- `actionExecutionHumanOwned: true`
+- `verificationEvidenceHumanRecorded: true`
+- `completionAcceptanceHumanRequired: true`
+- `repeatIncidentLinkageAdvisory: true`
+- `automaticCorrectiveActionExecution: false`
+- `automaticCompletion: false`
+- `autonomousProductionChanges: false`
+
+## Current authenticated runtime
+
+The untouched Chefs runtime does not yet contain accepted post-incident corrective actions.
+
+V50.25 therefore correctly reports:
+
+- status: `corrective-actions-required`
+- corrective actions: 0
+- automatic corrective-action execution: false
+- automatic completion: false
+- autonomous production changes: false
+
+The current demo owner account does not hold the admin permission required for corrective-action completion acceptance, and the attempted acceptance correctly returns HTTP 403.
+
+## Validation
+
+- V50.25 Production Learning & Corrective Action Governance lifecycle PASS
+- cross-incident corrective-action register PASS
+- owner / due-date aging PASS
+- overdue and high-risk classification PASS
+- repeat-incident advisory linkage PASS
+- risk-reduction evidence PASS
+- executive accountability rollup PASS
+- human verification PASS
+- human completion acceptance PASS
+- execution remains NOT_EXECUTED_BY_BLUE_CURRENT PASS
+- V50.20 Production Recovery regression PASS
+- authenticated governance GET PASS
+- admin completion-acceptance boundary PASS
+- authoritative database unchanged
+- npm run check PASS
+- 914 JavaScript files
+- 768 client scripts
+- 5,737 unique HTML IDs
+
+## Next
+
+V50.26–V50.30 should close and certify V50:
+
+- production handoff contract
+- production health/support contract
+- incident-command contract
+- recovery/post-incident contract
+- corrective-action governance contract
+- all human-control boundaries
+- full V50 regression
+- startup/UI/API certification
